      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address the signal-to-noise ratio, we can introduce a non-linear adaptive Kalman filter directly into the SDE to dynamically weight the variance spikes against the background market volatility. This filter will learn to suppress standard stochastic noise while amplifying the specific high-probability signatures you detect, effectively creating a \"signal gate\" that only opens when the local variance exceeds a critical threshold. By calibrating the filter's innovation term to your specific intuition, we ensure the model isolates the true pre-event spikes from the chaotic flux of the environment. Let's write the code to implement this adaptive filtering mechanism and test it on your latest data streams.",
      "source": "target",
